{"type":"message","id":"a5950720","parentId":"78fd2320","timestamp":"2026-05-27T12:29:08.090Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The wiki node listing is failing with 400. Let me check - the doc has 18 blocks with content (confirmed via API). But the user sees an empty page. This is very strange.\n\nWait - could it be that the doc was created but NOT linked to the wiki space properly? Earlier I had success adding it. But maybe it was added to the wrong place or the link is broken.\n\nActually, looking at the image again - the watermark says \"嘟吨 1731\". This is a standard Feishu watermark for confidential documents. The doc exists.\n\nBut the content isn't showing. The fact that API shows 18 blocks with content means the content IS there. \n\nSo Feishu is rendering the doc with 18 blocks including the title and content blocks, but the user sees nothing - which suggests a rendering issue rather than a data problem. I'm wondering if those appended blocks ended up inside the wrong parent block instead of at the document root, though that shouldn't happen with the API since it specifies the parent as the doc itself. Let me look at the block structure more carefully to see if the block_type values are correct.\n\nBlock type 1 is \"page\", block type 2 is \"text\" - those are right. But I need to check whether the blocks are actually nested inside each other rather than sitting at the root level. The page block itself (AdlIdY86Eo3rL6xnKz6c8aranRg) has block_type=1, which is the page. All the text blocks have block_type=2. In Feishu, the page structure should be: Page (type=1) > text blocks (type=2) as children. But could the \"index\" parameter have caused them to be inserted inside the page block itself?\n\nLooking at the append response - \"index\": 999999 was used, but actually it wasn't included in the final code that ran. The API returned successfully and added 11 blocks. But if the API succeeded and the blocks are there, why is the UI showing empty? I'm wondering if those 11 blocks are actually nested inside the page block as children rather than at the document root. In Feishu's block model, the document contains blocks, but maybe there's a container block I'm missing. Let me try fetching the blocks again with expanded pagination to see the full hierarchy.\n","thinkingSignature":"87c996f921054cdbec0c827ae4560ce9546f64d9be13a111f46a84fa438438d9"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_64qdh1jos7xy_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport urllib.request, json\nwith open('/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json') as f: config = json.load(f)\nfeishu = config['channels']['feishu']['accounts']['main']\nreq = urllib.request.Request('https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal',\n    data=json.dumps({'app_id': feishu['appId'], 'app_secret': feishu['appSecret']}).encode(),\n    headers={'Content-Type': 'application/json'})\ntoken = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req).read())['tenant_access_token']\n\ndoc_token = 'AdlIdY86Eo3rL6xnKz6c8aranRg'\n# Check block types more carefully\nreq2 = urllib.request.Request(\n    f'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{doc_token}/blocks?page_size=100',\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}'})\nr = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req2).read())\nfor item in r.get('data', {}).get('items', []):\n    bt = item.get('block_type')\n    parent_id = item.get('parent_id', '')\n    block_id = item.get('block_id', '')\n    print(f'{block_id} parent={parent_id} type={bt}')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":592,"output":795,"cacheRead":51168,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":52555,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779884939257,"responseId":"0666168b5b3d78a91279bb22d72ec82d"}}
