{"type":"message","id":"e79ee162","parentId":"1e75e350","timestamp":"2026-05-27T12:31:51.508Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"chat:oc_76f7651cb976ad84d66158beb2f29be2\",\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6e5a0dd9c0a0c294df929cf81bc\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_b86993389daaac2c0d8dc372341a20f7\",\n  \"conversation_label\": \"Robot Space 【 多Agent 群聊空间】\",\n  \"sender\": \"ou_b86993389daaac2c0d8dc372341a20f7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-05-27 12:31 UTC\",\n  \"group_subject\": \"Robot Space 【 多Agent 群聊空间】\",\n  \"is_group_chat\": true,\n  \"was_mentioned\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"ou_b86993389daaac2c0d8dc372341a20f7\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_b86993389daaac2c0d8dc372341a20f7\",\n  \"name\": \"ou_b86993389daaac2c0d8dc372341a20f7\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6e5a0dd9c0a0c294df929cf81bc]\nou_b86993389daaac2c0d8dc372341a20f7: 这个是空的 啊，没有看见你写入任何内容啊\n\n[System: The content may include mention tags in the form <at user_id=\"...\">name</at>. Treat these as real mentions of Feishu entities (users or bots).]\n[System: If user_id is \"ou_2801ea23f2cb858013a8191ad646d332\", that mention refers to you.]"}],"timestamp":1779885111475}}
{"type":"message","id":"90d10abd","parentId":"e79ee162","timestamp":"2026-05-27T12:32:02.854Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"哪吒说新链接还是空的。This is very strange. The API returns success but the content doesn't show in the UI. Let me think about what could be wrong.\n\nWait - let me re-read what happened. The issue might be that I'm creating blocks as children of the document but they might be going to the wrong parent block. Each document has a root block (type 1), and I should add children to that root block.\n\nIn the Feishu docx API:\n- `POST /open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{document_id}/blocks/{block_id}/children` - add children to a specific block\n- The {block_id} for the document root is the document_id itself\n\n\n- When creating a new docx document, the first block is always type=1 (the document root/title block)\n\nI'm definitely using the correct block_id parameter, and the new document is a fresh docx without any blocks yet. But if the document root is a type=1 block, I can't add children to it - I need to add blocks at the document level, not as children of the root.\n\nLet me reconsider the structure. In Feishu, paragraphs are block_type=2 and they should be added as direct children of the document root. But the problem might be that I'm passing the wrong block_id when trying to add blocks - the API expects a valid block_id that already exists in the document. I'm wondering if the issue is that the blocks aren't actually children of the root block like they should be, and I need to verify their actual hierarchy. Maybe the token is cached and my new blocks are being saved in a session that hasn't synced to the server yet, though that seems unlikely after waiting over a minute. Let me try creating a fresh document with a new title to see if that resolves the issue.\n\nLooking at the API response, the blocks were successfully added to the document, yet the UI shows nothing. This suggests the blocks might exist in the database but aren't being displayed correctly—possibly because text blocks require both block_type=2 and text content in a specific format. When I created the new document, it has a default title block, so I need to check whether the blocks I'm adding are actually children of the document root or if they're orphaned somewhere.\n\nThe problem might be that blocks have a hierarchical structure where type=2 blocks must be nested inside type=1 container blocks, not direct children of the document root itself. I'm realizing the document root is block_type=1 with the document_id as its block_id, so my paragraph blocks should be added as children of that root block. But looking at the response where 18 blocks were added, I'm wondering if I'm actually creating paragraphs or nested blocks instead—maybe I need to reconsider whether the structure should be different, with type=2 blocks going somewhere else entirely.\n\nLet me take a different approach: instead of trying to add blocks to the root, I'll create the document fresh, add a single paragraph using the simplest possible block structure, and verify it actually appears in the UI before scaling up to more complex content.\n\nLooking at the original code that worked when I first created the Talus doc, it used the same endpoint but positioned the new blocks at index=0 instead of appending them. The API docs suggest that when index=0, new children are inserted before the existing first child of the parent block, so maybe the issue is that I need to explicitly specify the index parameter rather than relying on the default behavior.\n\nNow I understand why the original approach failed—it deleted 261 blocks and added 48 new ones, which caused the overwrite. For the new document with 21 blocks showing no content, I'm wondering if the block_id passed to the children endpoint is wrong, since the document_id itself serves as the root block_id in Feishu's docx API. I'm wondering if blocks might need a parent_id field to render properly, even though the API should automatically set the parent when I call the children endpoint. Let me just try a different approach entirely—writing the content using Feishu's raw content API instead, which might be more reliable than reconstructing the block structure from scratch.","thinkingSignature":"7848bd0e776bf285a9db5fb1066f5479921b11fdb44d857cffb12ab2af335fa1"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_xejgwejd89jq_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport urllib.request, json\nwith open('/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json') as f: config = json.load(f)\nfeishu = config['channels']['feishu']['accounts']['main']\nreq = urllib.request.Request('https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal',\n    data=json.dumps({'app_id': feishu['appId'], 'app_secret': feishu['appSecret']}).encode(),\n    headers={'Content-Type': 'application/json'})\ntoken = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req).read())['tenant_access_token']\n\n# Create fresh doc with 1 simple paragraph\nreq2 = urllib.request.Request('https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents',\n    data=json.dumps({'title': 'Talus Test Simple'}).encode(),\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'})\nnew_doc = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req2).read())['data']['document']['document_id']\n\n# Add as wiki node\nspace_id = 7642970390779661243\nreq3 = urllib.request.Request(f'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/wiki/v2/spaces/{space_id}/nodes',\n    data=json.dumps({\n        'node_type': 'origin', 'obj_type': 'docx', 'obj_token': new_doc,\n        'title': 'Talus Test Simple', 'parent_node_token': 'G96wwD6IXiDlTQkiNK8cnfEonjh'\n    }).encode(),\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'})\nr3 = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req3).read())\nprint('wiki add:', r3.get('code'), r3.get('msg', ''))\n\n# Write 1 paragraph as child of doc root\nblock = {'block_type': 2, 'text': {'elements': [{'text_run': {'content': 'Test paragraph - is this visible?'}}]}}\nreq4 = urllib.request.Request(\n    f'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{new_doc}/blocks/{new_doc}/children',\n    data=json.dumps({'children': [block]}).encode(),\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'})\nr4 = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req4).read())\nprint('write result:', r4.get('code'), r4.get('msg', ''))\nchildren = r4.get('data', {}).get('children', [])\nprint('children added:', len(children))\nif children:\n    print('first child id:', children[0].get('block_id'))\n    print('first child type:', children[0].get('block_type'))\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":6072,"output":1470,"cacheRead":48544,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":56086,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779885111554,"responseId":"06661738b557b042289b61c7c03798bd"}}
