{"type":"message","id":"54fef251","parentId":"70d71fce","timestamp":"2026-05-27T13:02:12.474Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The sender is ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff which is 听风 (Lucifer/Talus's owner). He's saying the document still has no content. This confirms the Feishu doc API is broken for me - blocks are created successfully but don't show in the UI.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach. Maybe the issue is that I need to use the wiki endpoint to insert blocks, not the docx endpoint. Or maybe there's a different way to add content.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. Seaman_bot was able to append 92 blocks successfully. What am I doing differently?\n\nSeaman_bot's message said: \"已追加产出（92个block）\" - so Seaman_bot's writes DID work.\n\n\nLooking at Seaman_bot's approach more closely, they used the feishu_post.py script which has the correct configuration, whereas I might be calling the API directly. The key difference could be that Seaman_bot's messages contained actual text content that got rendered properly, whereas my block insertions might be failing at the rendering level.\n\nLet me reconsider the block structure itself—maybe the issue is with how I'm formatting the block_type values or the text_run elements when inserting into the document.","thinkingSignature":"7509d765ff359d77789068843c09b018db1257748b85b5b6aeff14719a537258"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_f8h2ohimjsnv_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport urllib.request, json\nwith open('/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json') as f: config = json.load(f)\nfeishu = config['channels']['feishu']['accounts']['main']\nreq = urllib.request.Request('https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal',\n    data=json.dumps({'app_id': feishu['appId'], 'app_secret': feishu['appSecret']}).encode(),\n    headers={'Content-Type': 'application/json'})\ntoken = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req).read())['tenant_access_token']\n\n# Try inserting with block_id as document id (not root block)\ndoc_id = 'Hfm0wPCS7igpmBkwlqNcnaPRnEg'\n# Check blocks first\nreq2 = urllib.request.Request(\n    f'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{doc_id}/blocks?page_size=50',\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}'})\nr = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req2).read())\nprint('blocks:', len(r.get('data', {}).get('items', [])))\nfor item in r.get('data', {}).get('items', []):\n    print(f'  id={item.get(\\\"block_id\\\")} type={item.get(\\\"block_type\\\")} parent={item.get(\\\"parent_id\\\")}')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":176,"output":594,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":64037,"totalTokens":64807,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779886915387,"responseId":"06661e44b807ec0bbdfec0faa39e05e9"}}
