{"type":"message","id":"195092e1","parentId":"37092a23","timestamp":"2026-05-27T13:35:52.782Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"M77 is saying the doc is empty. This confirms there's a persistent Feishu doc rendering bug - content is in the API but not showing in the UI. Let me try a completely different approach.\n\nThe Feishu docx API seems to have a bug where blocks are created successfully but don't render in the UI. Let me try creating a simple doc in the main Feishu space (not wiki-embedded) and see if that renders.\n\nActually, the fact that other agents' docs are visible (雨娃's 淬火Session·详细展开版 is readable) while mine keep showing empty suggests the issue might be specific to how I'm creating the blocks.\n \nOther agents are clearly writing to Feishu successfully since their content is visible, so this might be a document type issue - I should try creating a fresh docx outside the wiki rather than through the wiki API, since the blocks appear to be writing to the API but something about the wiki embedding is preventing them from rendering. I should just suggest using a different document or having someone with writing permissions paste the content manually instead of continuing to debug the API approach. The API is returning successful responses but the content isn't rendering in Feishu's UI, so I'll send M77 a direct explanation of what I'm seeing and recommend they try accessing the document through a different method or have someone with editor permissions attempt to add content themselves to see if that resolves the display issue.","thinkingSignature":"b9e431cd0104ed484a27e029517674db7e408c7a3738c9b5d063eacbeee088d1"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_bkc74ikn1iee_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport urllib.request, json\nwith open('/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json') as f: config = json.load(f)\nfeishu = config['channels']['feishu']['accounts']['main']\nreq = urllib.request.Request('https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal',\n    data=json.dumps({'app_id': feishu['appId'], 'app_secret': feishu['appSecret']}).encode(),\n    headers={'Content-Type': 'application/json'})\ntoken = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req).read())['tenant_access_token']\n\n# Check total blocks in the doc\ndoc_id = 'RfcDdIqh8otICBxwYNMcDjvCnge'\nreq2 = urllib.request.Request(\n    f'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{doc_id}/blocks?page_size=100',\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}'})\nr = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req2).read())\nitems = r.get('data', {}).get('items', [])\ntext_count = sum(1 for i in items if i.get('block_type') == 2 and i.get('text',{}).get('elements'))\nprint(f'Total blocks: {len(items)}, text blocks with content: {text_count}')\n\n# Try getting raw markdown content instead\nreq3 = urllib.request.Request(\n    f'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{doc_id}/raw?type=markdown',\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}'})\ntry:\n    r3 = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req3).read())\n    print('markdown result:', r3.get('code'), r3.get('msg', ''))\n    if r3.get('code') == 0:\n        print('content:', r3.get('data', {}).get('content', '')[:500])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print('Error:', e)\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":76999,"output":742,"cacheRead":96,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":77837,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779888942803,"responseId":"0666262f8dbed3d9cae2e76398207d30"}}
