{"type":"message","id":"64672bc7","parentId":"4902f69a","timestamp":"2026-05-27T13:40:05.458Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The content is definitely in the API - 63 blocks, 62 text blocks. The first block is \"TALUS TEST - is this visible?\" and subsequent blocks contain the actual content.\n\nThe issue is a Feishu Docs rendering problem. The content exists in the API but doesn't show in the UI. This could be because:\n1. The document was created via API and needs to be opened in the editor to trigger rendering\n2. There's a caching issue\n3. The wiki embedding causes rendering issues\n\nThe fact that M77 said \"TALUS TEST\" showed up but the rest didn't is interesting - it suggests maybe the first few blocks render but then stop. Or maybe M77 was looking at a different state.\n \nI'm wondering if the issue is specific to this document or a broader Feishu problem - maybe the wiki version has rendering problems while the direct doc link works better. But if听风 confirmed even the direct link is blank despite the content being there, this seems like a known Feishu limitation where documents created or modified via API don't render properly in the UI until someone's opened them in the editor. The user might just need to open the document in Feishu Docs to trigger rendering.\n\nActually, I'm noticing something odd -听风 said the direct doc link showed only \"TALUS TEST\" as blank, but M77 was able to see it. This suggests different users might be seeing different rendering states. Let me try a completely different approach: I'll create a new document manually through Feishu and then attempt to write to it via the API to see if that resolves the rendering issue.","thinkingSignature":"78fc660fbc37fce61ef3ab744f7f0662f3b614433981b1d7b6c6d04544ca8320"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_2wtap48vujgh_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport urllib.request, json\n\nwith open('/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json') as f: config = json.load(f)\nfeishu = config['channels']['feishu']['accounts']['main']\nreq = urllib.request.Request('https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal',\n    data=json.dumps({'app_id': feishu['appId'], 'app_secret': feishu['appSecret']}).encode(),\n    headers={'Content-Type': 'application/json'})\ntoken = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req).read())['tenant_access_token']\n\n# Try using batch update - maybe there's a pending state issue\ndoc_id = 'VI8YdL2Lton1vUx2GR0cu8FCnDb'\n\n# Try to trigger a flush by doing a trivial update\nblock = {'block_type': 2, 'text': {'elements': [{'text_run': {'content': '--- 内容已写入，请向下滚动查看完整淬火Session记录 ---'}}]}}\nreq2 = urllib.request.Request(\n    f'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{doc_id}/blocks/{doc_id}/children',\n    data=json.dumps({'children': [block], 'index': 1}).encode(),\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'})\nr = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req2).read())\nprint('flush attempt:', r.get('code'), r.get('msg', ''))\n\n# Verify\nreq3 = urllib.request.Request(\n    f'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{doc_id}/blocks?page_size=10',\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}'})\nr3 = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req3).read())\nfor item in r3.get('data', {}).get('items', [])[:5]:\n    if item.get('block_type') == 2:\n        try:\n            txt = ' '.join([e.get('text_run',{}).get('content','') for el in item.get('text',{}).get('elements',[]) for e in [el] if e.get('text_run',{}).get('content','')])\n            print(f'  {txt[:60]}')\n        except: pass\nPYEOF"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":76204,"output":861,"cacheRead":26004,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":103069,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779889186091,"responseId":"066627222d93fd45b3626490